d to the  true horrors of yharnam and as you  progress through the game these cosmic  beings or great ones become visible to  you bloodborne is very similar to the  souls games in a number of ways but when  it comes to combat it's a completely  different  beast  while souls promotes a more measured  cautious approach blocking and waiting  for openings from behind a shield  bloodborne encourages aggression when  you're hit by an enemy a short window  opens where doing damage to the person  that hit you gives you back health  pushing the player to attack rather than  cower and regroup your weapons now  transform and stacking combos together  feels fluid and powerful shields were  removed from the game well save one  wooden shield that calls you a coward  for picking it replacing it in your left  hand is a gun when fired at just the  right time it stuns the enemy and opens  them up for a visceral attack which  deals extra damage bloodborne was and  this may surprise you critically  acclaimed upon release and was quickly  referred to as the best playstation 4  exclusive game and a true killer app for  the console it was added to playstation  now and later to the playstation plus  collection on playstation 5 but still  nothing about a pc release a few months  after it came out it received a meaty  dlc expansion called the old hunters  which takes players back in time and up  against a whole host of new bosses  as with other souls games bloodborne's  difficulty was key to helping its  community grow not only were people  coming together to learn how to beat the  game normally it has a strong speed  running community with players figuring  out how to beat it in the fastest time  and even doing runs without taking any  hits bloodborne's cut content also  intrigued folks to come together to mine  every last secret they could from the  game its first trailer showed a lot of  mechanics and weapons that didn't  actually make it into the final product  and players have combed through its code  to uncover cut bosses locations and bits  of story it's been seven years since  bloodborne was released and people are  still finding things  dark souls 3 was to be a culmination of  everything from software had learned  while creating its other games directed  by miyazaki but co-directed by dark  souls 2's yuui tanimura and isamu okano  who had previously directed steel  battalion heavy armor and was a game  designer on bloodborne dark souls 3 was  to straddle the line of being both  familiar but pushed new ground for the  studio  speaking at e3 2015 miyazaki said that  dark souls 3 wouldn't be the final  product for the dark souls franchise but  instead act as a turning point for the  series and for from software as a whole  its story follows similar beats and  themes of the previous games and its  combat while very familiar to those who  had played previous souls games is a  little faster and dynamic archery was  much improved with miyazaki revealing  that the team at from was inspired by  legolas from lord of the rings the game  introduces a new stat luck and weapon  arts special skills that can give you  the edge in a fight like breaking an  enemy's guard or dealing more damage  dark souls 3 aimed to encourage a  greater sense of exploration its map was  bigger but also fairly interconnected in  a way that fans had loved in dark souls  and bloodborne despite some technical  issues and a rough frame rate at launch  it was very well received by fans and  critics who emboldened by their  experience with bloodborne and its  aggressive combat praised the faster  fights in dark souls 3 as well as the  gorgeous world of lothric some  complained that the game didn't feel as  fresh or exciting as previous titles  lacking surprise and relying too heavily  on series mainstays regardless it was  the fastest selling game in bandai  namco's history and two pieces of dlc  the ringed city and ashes of ariandel  were released dark souls 3 might not  have moved the needle as much as some  souls fans hoped but from software's  next game sakura shadows died twice  would be a vast departure for the studio  an action-adventure game more in line  with tenchu than dark souls  as it's not a soulsborne i'll not dwell  on it too much but it's really fun to  chart the changes the studio made to its  games as their approach to game design  evolved over time  which brings us to eldon ring which  looks to be a culmination and evolution  of these soulsborne games so far taking  the core tenets of dark souls and  setting players loose in an expansive  open world and letting them make their  own path a song of ice and fire author  george r.r martin contributed to the  game's law with miyazaki taking up the  reigns as director once again  new is the ability to ride a mount a  spectral steed named torrent as well as  crafting using materials you've gathered  from enemies and the environment the  lands between it looks to be huge and  players need to collect map shards to  unfog the map to explore not only can  you play cooperatively with people  online but in certain areas you can  summon spirit ashes spectral beings that  attack enemies for you borrowing from  sakura you can stealth through various  areas and even jump offering more ways  to dispatch enemies elden ring has been  delayed a couple of times but is finally  launching in 2022 and i can't wait  so there you have it the history of  soulsborne games for more from software  make sure to keep your eyes peeled to  gamespot and be sure to let me know  which one is your favorite in the  comments below you can find me on  twitter i'm at lucy james games and  thanks for watching
 

